---
layout: layouts/base.njk
templateEngineOverride: njk
---

{#- The publishing strip, as on every other entry. A photograph is a mark in
    the register like any other, so it shows where it sits. -#}
{%- set pulse = collections.allContent | pulseMonths(0) | collapseEmptyYears(timelineGaps) %}
{%- set pulseCurrentKey = date | dateDisplay('yyyy-LL') %}
{% include "partials/pulse-strip.njk" %}

<article class="kh-u-margin__top--1200">
  {#- The photograph is the content, not an illustration of it, so the figure
      sits outside the reading column below, spanning the full grid the way
      post.njk's hero does not. Sizing lives in _kh-photos.scss. -#}
  <figure class="kh-photo__figure">
    {#- width/height are this image's own intrinsic size, hardcoded because the
        eleventy-img transform does not process this tag (site-wide, not fixed
        here). They must change with the image; without them the browser
        reserves no space and the full-width hero shifts the page as it loads. -#}
    <img class="kh-photo__img" src="/images{{ image | url }}"
         alt="{{ image_meta.altext or image_meta.alt or '' }}"
         width="2000" height="1500"
         decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
  </figure>

  {#- The caption sits in the same reading column every other entry uses, via
      the same `kh-grid-stylized` wrapper and empty leading div that
      digesting.njk has. It was previously a plain block, which pinned the text
      to the page's left edge under a centred photograph; the mismatch read as
      a bug. The figure stays outside this wrapper, because the photograph is
      the one thing here that genuinely wants the full width. -#}
  <div class="kh-grid-stylized">
    <div></div>
    <div class="kh-content">
    <p class="kh-breadcrumb" data-pagefind-ignore><a href="/photos/">← Photos</a></p>
    <h1 class="kh-font-headline kh-text-heading--1">{{ title }}</h1>
    {#- Parents only, and linked when a topic page exists, matching
        digesting.njk. Without this a topic page would list the photograph
        while the photograph never linked back. -#}
    <p class="kh-meta" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <time datetime="{{ date }}">{{ date | dateDisplay }}</time>
      {%- if photo_meta and photo_meta.place %} &middot; {{ photo_meta.place }}{% endif %}
      {%- if topics %} &middot; Filed in:
        {%- for parent in topics | topicParents %}
        {%- set topicSlug = collections.topics | topicPageSlug(parent) %}
        {% if topicSlug %}<a href="/topics/{{ topicSlug }}/">{{ parent }}</a>{% else %}{{ parent }}{% endif %}{{ "," if not loop.last }}
        {%- endfor %}
      {%- endif %}
    </p>
    {% if image_meta and image_meta.text %}
    <p>{{ image_meta.text | safe }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {{ content | safe }}
    {#- Apparatus, not content: the credit and the exposure line would otherwise
        be indexed as body text and surface as search excerpts. -#}
    <p class="kh-meta kh-photo__tech" data-pagefind-ignore>
      {%- if image_meta and image_meta.credit %}{{ image_meta.credit | safe }}{% endif %}
      {%- if photo_meta and photo_meta.camera %} {{ photo_meta.camera | safe }}{% endif %}
      {%- if photo_meta and photo_meta.taken %} &middot; {{ photo_meta.taken }}{% endif %}
      {#- Latitude and longitude are two frontmatter fields rather than one
          "lat, lon" string because Nunjucks has no `split` filter here, so a
          single string could be printed but never taken apart to build the
          map URL. Two fields also leave the numbers machine-readable. -#}
      {%- if photo_meta and photo_meta.lat and photo_meta.lon %} &middot;
      <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat={{ photo_meta.lat }}&amp;mlon={{ photo_meta.lon }}#map=17/{{ photo_meta.lat }}/{{ photo_meta.lon }}">{{ photo_meta.lat }}, {{ photo_meta.lon }}</a>
      {%- endif %}
    </p>
    <p><a href="/photos/">More photos</a></p>
    {%- if comment != false %}
    {% include "partials/feedback.njk" %}
    {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</article>

{#- The same closing block as every other entry: byline, related entries and
    the sequence rail, so a photograph reached from a link is not a dead end. -#}
{% include "partials/entry-foot.njk" %}
